It is Sunday afternoon.
I am sitting on a bench in the park.
I am eating a warm bun maska.
Moti is sitting near my feet.
He is looking at me with big, sad eyes.
He wants my food.
But giving human food to dogs is forbidden.
I tell him firmly, "No, Moti."
"Do not look at it."
Moti is my neighbor Asha's dog.
Asha's rule is very strict.
"You must not eat this."
Moti whines softly.
I feel a little bad.
I take out a dog biscuit from my bag.
"Sit, Moti," I say.
He sits down immediately.
I give him the biscuit.
"Now eat it," I say.
He eats his biscuit happily.
And I eat my bun maska comfortably.
